{number: 20}
{title: Jesus Is All the World to Me}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Jesus is all the world to me, my [F] life, my joy, my [C] all;
He is my strength from day to day, with-[G] out Him I would [C] fall.
When I am sad to [Am] Him I go, no [F] other one can [G] cheer me so;
When [C] I am sad He makes me glad, He’s [F] my [G] Fri-[C] end.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Jesus is all the world to me, my [F] Friend in trials [C] sore;
I go to Him for blessings, and He [G] gives them o’er and [C] o’er.
He sends the sunshine [Am] and the rain, He [F] sends the harvest’s [G] golden grain;
Sun-[C] shine and rain, harvest of grain, He’s [F] my [G] Fri-[C] end.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Jesus is all the world to me, and [F] true to Him I’ll [C] be;
O, how could I this Friend deny, when [G] He’s so true to [C] me?
Following Him I [Am] know I’m right, He [F] watches o’er me [G] day and night;
Fol-[C] lowing Him by day and night, He’s [F] my [G] Fri-[C] end.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[C] Jesus is all the world to me, I [F] want no better [C] friend;
I trust Him now, I’ll trust Him when life’s [G] fleeting days shall [C] end.
Beautiful life with [Am] such a Friend; beau-[F] tiful life that [G] has no end;
E-[C] ternal life, eternal joy, He’s [F] my [G] Fri-[C] end.
{end_of_verse}
